	"notes": [
		{
			"id": "ny9-9jAKAGRTTytur",
			"text": "Typical Stats from the package record: ST 13, DX 14, IQ 3, HT 12, HP 13, WILL 8, PER 10, FP 12, SPEED 6.5, MOVE 6, DODGE 9, DR 1. GCS derives its own values by applying the ancestry; where the two differ, the package's Typical Stats are what the Dungeons on Automatic encounter tables use."
		},
		{
			"id": "nSPdpm7V6YzCwRcu2",
			"text": "Encounter rating: CER 22 (offense 15, protection 7), threat tier minor, appearing 4."
		},
		{
			"id": "n2nppxtNGe2_kyZBL",
			"text": "GCS ancestry draft: gcs/deinonychus.gct"
		},
		{
			"id": "n2zuhhfl1UwJBwDUM",
			"text": "Independent build total: -37 points of racial traits plus 14 points of racial skills."
		},
		{
			"id": "nNo1QHK8g8BqNrnG7",
			"text": "Answers the SRD heading(s): Deinonychus (SRD 3.5). Only the creature identity is taken from the SRD; the GURPS statistics, ratings and prose are this project's own work and reproduce no SRD text."
		},
		{
			"id": "ntDkIOZjxlx-SFREN",
			"text": "Typical Stats, damage and ratings are derived from the racial template, not authored beside it, so the sheet and the stat block cannot disagree."
		},
		{
			"id": "nvuP6pGVuB5Iz9tCk",
			"text": "Body mass used to scale this build: 70 kg. ST, Size Modifier and DR are checked against it; see the gurps-animal-sanity-check skill for the bands."
		},
		{
			"id": "n9CiXtRMuGza1lg72",
			"text": "Movement: ground Move 6, 9 at a sprint (primary). The published Move is the primary medium's cruising Move; sprint figures are stated here and not folded into it."
		},
		{
			"id": "nd3K8hwm-1eMStq27",
			"text": "Treasure and grappling are not authored for this batch and ship as explicit nulls; `lair` carries a short habitat note, because where a wandering animal dens is an encounter fact rather than a loot one."
		},
		{
			"id": "ntauq3UqBhxKSDFm_",
			"text": "About three metres nose to tail, which is the SM +1 row; most of that is tail."
		},
		{
			"id": "nwlBcG4siep1Ws8iT",
			"text": "ST from Basic Lift: it holds down and tears apart something its own size."
		},
		{
			"id": "n6-HW3UWN1Lu-KjeQ",
			"text": "The pack is the threat. Run these as a coordinated group."
		},
		{
			"id": "n7Fgp-VjB7ysikmr0",
			"text": "Added after a post-hoc comparison against independent GURPS fan conversions of this creature: the Tracking skill, which a creature with Discriminatory Smell should always have. The comparison surfaced the gap; the build is still ours."
		},
		{
			"id": "n2G9QNY0evMmGThL5",
			"text": "Monster statistics, ratings and description prose by Monsters on Automatic; AI-generated first draft, project-reviewed, released under CC BY 4.0."
		}
	],
